   "evidence": "`Diffractive/Basic.lean:98` `def MX2 (g : Bilin V) (K : ExclKinematics V)` vs `:74,:83,:90` `(K : DisKinematics V)`; roadmap `Diffraction/README.md:273-279` lists `\u0394 = P - P'`, `\u03be`, `\u03b2`, `M_X\u00b2 = (q + \u0394)\u00b2`, `M_Y\u00b2 = P'\u00b2` as variables of `q`, `P`, `P'` alone, with `:288` making that y-independence an explicit theorem of the layer.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Diffractive/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Define `MX2 (g : Bilin V) (K : DisKinematics V) : \u211d := g (K.q + (K.p - K.pPrime)) (K.q + (K.p - K.pPrime))` with the matching `MX2_def`, using the same inline `\u0394 = K.p - K.pPrime` as `xi`/`beta`. All four definitions then sit on one record, and `\u03b2 = Q\u00b2 / (Q\u00b2 + M_X\u00b2 \u2212 t)` becomes statable in this PR with `t` written inline as `g (K.p - K.pPrime) (K.p - K.pPrime)` \u2014 no bridge needed, so this does not reopen the scope rubric's block. Drop `MX2_eq_q_sub_delta_sq` and let the `M_X\u00b2 = q'\u00b2` identification land with the `ExclKinematics extends DisKinematics` PR.",
   "issue": "`MX2` takes `ExclKinematics V` while `xi`, `beta`, `MY2` take `DisKinematics V`. Nothing in the repo connects the two records (`ExclKinematics` at `Exclusive/Kinematics/Basic.lean:32` is standalone; `toDisKinematics` exists only for `PolarizedKinematics`), so the \u00a70.1 surface ships in two mutually unusable halves: no consumer can combine `M_X\u00b2` with `\u03be`, `\u03b2`, `M_Y\u00b2` or `x`. The roadmap defines `M_X\u00b2 = (q + \u0394)\u00b2` (README.md:279), a function of `q`, `P`, `P'` alone, exactly like the other three; the PR inverts this, making `q'\u00b2` the definition and the roadmap's defining form a derived lemma, which is what forces the record split.",
   "line": "98"
  }
